 functions as values, calls through locals, fields and pipes via call_indirect (selfhost/ir/lower_closure.pilot, stand-in ir.closure_record); declared operators (`op ==`) called on their type; `x |> .m()`; map literals typed as the type `bind_map_literal` names, with `m.key` reading key `key`; `*xs` and `*..xs` in list literals through the engine operation `bind_list_splat` names ; a function whose parameters carry no type lowered once per set of argument types it is called with, the loop element type following from the specialized iterable; a function returning different types returns their union (selfhost/ir/lower_union.pilot) as one record of tag then value, a method call on it switching on the tag, a list literal of different program structs holding their union, a bare call inside a method calling the sibling method (stand-in ir.engine_union_arg); top-level bindings as module globals and a `<start>` function that runs the user files' `comptime` code in source order, then the imported globals the program reads, then the top-level statements, then `main` (selfhost/ir/lower_global.pilot, stand-in ir.comptime_at_start); module-qualified calls (`io.read_line()`) and library bodies that are one engine operation; `nameof(x)`; dimensional literals (`250ms`, `3[ms]`) through the converter `bind_unit_literal` names (selfhost/ir/lower_unit.pilot, stand-in ir.unit_literal_call); cascades `..` / `?..` (method steps and field assignments); `Bundle.method(var ref self, ..)` delegation; property setters, guarded and typed, as one function per property and value type (selfhost/ir/lower_setter.pilot); destructuring `let` (tuple, slice with a rest, map record, struct shorthand; top level as globals) and slice and record `switch` patterns (selfhost/ir/lower_destructure.pilot); `x[a..b]` through `bind_range_index` (defer, try_catch, field_closure_call, pipes, types_clean, ir_closures_and_defer, if_some, fstring_quotes, collections, splat_list, for_enumerator, try_records, methods, ir_union_returns, globals_comptime, global_closures, const_map_len, modules, script_top_level, native_calls, stdin_lines, units, cascade, delegation, property_setters, guarded_setters, destructuring, json_rfc8259); `T(x)` on a string as a `cast` that fails at run time with the seed's error (err_convert_string); `x.name` on a register value as the seed's record read, which fails the same way (err_field_of_int); a failed destructuring and a value no setter takes end in `unreachable` carrying the seed's trap message (err_destructure_mismatch, err_setter_rejects); call-quote modes (`f!(..)`, `sig f(..)`, ..) end in `unreachable` carrying the seed's vm.call_quote seam message instead of lowering as a plain call (err_call_quote); `pilot test --ir` passes all 170 eligible conformance cases; a construct the lowering does not know still stops at ir.lower_construct", "ir.lower_construct ir.absent_as_null ir.engine_sequence_for ir.closure_record ir.engine_union_arg ir.comptime_at_start ir.unit_literal_call"),
        cap("F5", "verifier with its own dominators: IR001 (definition dominates use), IR002 (branch arity), IR003 (terminators)", ::Wired,
            "selfhost/ir/verify.pilot (Cooper-Harvey-Kennedy over reverse postorder) runs before every `pilot ir` mode; cli_f5 malformed_ir_is_rejected_with_its_code (tests/ir/*.pir)", ""),
        cap("F5", "PilIR text printer and parser that round-trip byte for byte", ::Wired,
