        cap("F5", "PilIR interpreter (`pilot ir run`)", ::Draft,
            "selfhost/ir/interp.pilot: one handler per opcode; operators, branch conditions, casts and engine operations run through the seed's own operation by name (engine op `op_checked`, crates/pilot-vm/src/checked.rs), which hands back the seed's failure message; a failure, a global read before its declaration ran, or `unreachable` stops the program with the seed's report (selfhost/ir/fault.pilot: `<file>:<line>:<col>: runtime error: ..`, then `called from` lines, exit 1; err_divide_by_zero, err_global_before_set, err_seam, err_pending); `pilot ir run <file> -- args` gives the program its script arguments (script_args); runs lowered programs with the seed's output (pilot test --ir) and hand-written IR with block-parameter loops (tests/ir/loop_params.pir); records are shared, not copied; call_indirect calls the function a function record names; module globals (`global_addr`, read and written with load/store) are shared by every frame (cli_f5 module_globals_are_shared_by_every_function, tests/ir/globals.pir); print with several arguments, assert, and standard input and script arguments through std.io and std.env (native_calls, stdin_lines)", "ir.interp_opcode ir.interp_hook ir.aggregate_by_reference ir.engine_sequence_for ir.absent_as_null ir.closure_record"),
