        cap("F5b", "generator functions (`yield`, next/send/close, `yield *xs`) on the seed and in PilIR", ::Draft,
            "stdlib/core/generator.pilot `Generator<TItem, TSent = void>` bound by `bind_generator`; the checker gives a function or lambda whose `yield` no collecting `for` owns the generator type (selfhost/check/generators.pilot, generic parameter defaults) and reports GEN001 (orphan `yield`), GEN002 (generator returning a value), GEN003 is the run-time error of resuming a running generator; the seed runs generator bodies as engine frames without threads (crates/pilot-vm lower_yield.rs, vm_gen.rs); PilIR lowers each generator to a function building its frame record and a resume function dispatching on the frame's state with switch_table, with the values live across a `yield` moved into the frame (selfhost/ir/lower_generator.pilot); `for` closes an enumerator that declares `close` on every exit, so leaving a loop over a generator runs its pending `defer`s; `yield splat(xs)` lowers to the same delegation as `yield *xs`; pilot run, pilot test --ir and pilot test --emit python/js: generator_count, generator_send, generator_delegate, generator_delegate_readable, generator_defer, generator_local, generator_lambda, err_gen_orphan_yield, err_gen_return_value, err_gen_item_type, err_gen_resume_self", "seed.generator_frame ir.closure_record"),
        cap("F5b", "collecting `for` expressions (`let ys = for .. { yield e; }`)", ::Draft,
