        cap("F7", "`var ref` exclusive arguments (ALIAS001)", ::Wired,
            "selfhost/check/aliasing.pilot: a place lent to a `var` parameter (`var ref x`) that another argument or the receiver of the same call also reaches (same root binding, overlapping field and element steps; an index that is not an integer literal may be any element) is ALIAS001; a plain parameter is the default borrow (`in`); tests/conformance/memory/alias_iso_params, err_alias_var_ref on pilot test, --ir and --emit c. The parser records each parameter modifier as its own flag (PARAM_FLAG_REF/MUT/ISO/COMPTIME, read by selfhost/check/snapshot.pilot param_flag); assigning a `var ref` parameter reaches the caller's variable: the seed hands each one's final value back at return (crates/pilot-vm SetOut/GetOut, lower_args.rs) and PilIR returns a record of the result and those values (selfhost/ir/lower_outs.pilot), tests/conformance/memory/var_ref_writeback on pilot test, --ir and --emit c. Phase 2: C `restrict`", ""),
        cap("F7", "`iso` isolated arguments (ISO001)", ::Wired,
            "selfhost/check/aliasing.pilot: an argument of an `iso` parameter that is a field or element of another value, a global, a parameter the caller was only lent, a view, passed twice in the call, borrowed by a binding used after the call, or itself used after the call (before a new value is assigned to it) is ISO001; a fresh value is accepted; tests/conformance/memory/alias_iso_params, err_iso_arg on pilot test, --ir and --emit c. The parser records each parameter modifier as its own flag (PARAM_FLAG_REF/MUT/ISO/COMPTIME, read by selfhost/check/snapshot.pilot param_flag); `iso` on a `let` binding is not checked", ""),
        cap("F4", "`assume(cond)` and `unreachable()` hints (HINT001, HINT002)", ::Wired,
